            "source_notes": "Volume % of coarse fragments larger than 2 mm: the property list of every dataset report says 'coarse fragments (> 2 mm, volume %)' (ISRIC Reports 2003/04 p.6, 2004/01 p.7, 2004/03 p.7, 2004/04 p.5, 2004/06 p.8, 2005/02 p.4, 2005/04 p.5, 2007/02 p.7, 2008/05 p.8, 2010/01 p.8, 2010/07b p.5); the summary-file tables write 'vol. % > 2 mm' (2008/05 p.29, 2010/01 p.29, 2010/07b p.23), '% > 2mm' (2007/02 p.24) or no unit (the other seven). SOVEUR v1: the shapefile has no unit, its readme refers to Report 2005/04 (version 2.0), whose values it repeats; the GeoNetwork metadata of v1 writes 'coarse fragments (less than 2 mm)', the opposite size class. Mapped to the volumetric property since 2026-10-13 (the hub catalog had it gravimetric); values unchanged."
